- {"id": "F1", "severity": "high", "path": "tools/drive_index.py:513", "evidence": "active_check requests the names of every live folder under _ACTIVE before applying HEALTH filtering. A health folder is therefore listed through the API, contrary to the stated restriction. In addition, an active board row whose name matches HEALTH remains in active_drift's active dictionary and can be printed as a missing row, including DexaProject.", "fix": "Exclude health names from the Drive query where possible and filter health-matching board rows before constructing or printing drift results. Ensure errors and diagnostic output cannot expose those names."}
- {"id": "F2", "severity": "high", "path": "tools/active_folders.py:44", "evidence": "children requests only files and neither requests nor follows nextPageToken. Drive may return a partial or empty page even when further pages exist. An existing matching folder or shortcut on a later page is then treated as absent and --apply creates a duplicate.", "fix": "Request nextPageToken and exhaust every page, failing closed if any page lookup fails, before deciding that a name is free."}
- {"id": "F3", "severity": "medium", "path": "tools/drive_index.py:491", "evidence": "seen maps each board name to a single folder, overwriting earlier matches. Two folders such as 2026-10-01_A and 2026-10-02_A can consequently produce zero drift when drive_folder points to the last one returned. An undated folder named A is also accepted as the matching folder if drive_folder points to it, despite the required dated name.", "fix": "Retain all folders per board name, report duplicates explicitly, and require a valid dated prefix for a folder to satisfy a board row."}
- {"id": "F4", "severity": "medium", "path": "tools/drive_index.py:506", "evidence": "active_check uses the indexed _ACTIVE ID without checking its live ancestry. If that folder was moved or renamed after the index was built, the command compares its old contents and can report a match while the intended 01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE location is missing or contains different folders.", "fix": "Verify the indexed folder's live path before listing its children and fail closed if it no longer matches the expected path."}
- {"id": "F5", "severity": "medium", "path": "tools/active_folders.py:66", "evidence": "The creation log is buffered and is never explicitly flushed after each successful creation. If the process is interrupted after Drive creates an item but before the buffer is written, its ID can be absent from the documented undo log; a rerun reuses that item and does not add the missing log entry.", "fix": "Keep an explicit log file handle and flush each successful creation record immediately; use durable syncing if the undo record must survive a machine failure."}
- {"id": "F6", "severity": "medium", "path": "tools/active_folders.py:62", "evidence": "The creation plan is hard-coded and never reconciled with the current portfolio. If a planned row becomes inactive before --apply, the tool still creates its folder; if a new row becomes active, the tool does not create one. active-check directs missing rows to this tool, but it can silently select no plan entry and report success.", "fix": "Read the current board before applying, validate every selected plan entry against an active row, and fail clearly for active rows or requested names that have no applicable plan."}
